title: fip-mcp
message: >-
  If you use fip-mcp, please cite it using the metadata in this file.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Fouilloux
    given-names: Anne
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1784-2920
    affiliation: LifeWatch ERIC
repository-code: https://github.com/ScienceLiveHub/fip-mcp
url: https://sciencelive4all.org
abstract: >-
  An MCP server that turns community FAIR Implementation Profiles (FIPs),
  published as nanopublications, into guidance and deterministic compliance
  checks for AI agents. An agent asks the FIP what the community agreed before
  it suggests a repository, format, licence or vocabulary, and can check a
  folder or a Zenodo record against the FIP. Verdicts are computed by code;
  resources that cannot be tested are reported as manual, and questions the
  community left open are reported as gaps. Developed in the OSCARS-FIESTA
  project (EU Horizon Europe grant 101129751) and maintained by the Science
  Live community.
keywords:
  - FAIR
  - FAIR Implementation Profile
  - FIP
  - nanopublications
